WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.242
To follow a patient's observations over time,

1.2
00:00:03.242 --> 00:00:06.667
open the encounter and select the Plots tab.

2.1
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:11.147
Select the sub-tab of a chart set, here Primary Parameters.

2.2
00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:14.299
The first chart set opens by default.

3.1
00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:20.198
Read a chart. Each chart opens on Graph, which draws one line for each code.

3.2
00:00:20.198 --> 00:00:25.455
Select Recent Data or Full History to see the values as a table.

4.1
00:00:25.455 --> 00:00:29.575
Select the title of a chart to open its history panel.

4.2
00:00:29.575 --> 00:00:35.449
Under the title, it shows All Encounters and the count, here 14 recordings.

5.1
00:00:35.449 --> 00:00:37.639
Choose the encounters to show.

5.2
00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:42.164
Select Show current encounter recordings to show only this encounter's

5.3
00:00:42.164 --> 00:00:47.190
observations, and clear it to show all the patient's encounters again.

6.1
00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.871
In the history panel, the Plots tab draws one chart for each code.

6.2
00:00:51.871 --> 00:00:56.534
Point at a value to see its details, including who entered it.

7.1
00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.749
Select the Table tab of the history panel.

7.2
00:00:59.749 --> 00:01:05.403
It has one row for each code, and one column for each time, newest first.
